There is no single objective “best” French cheese for the first quarter of the 21st century, but **Époisses Perrière** is a strong candidate because it was crowned “Best Cheese in the World” in 2023 at the Mondial du Fromage competition.[3][5]

If the question is about long-term popularity rather than a contest title, **Comté** is also a top contender: it is one of the most widely admired French cheeses in consumer preference studies and remains a benchmark among French cheeses.[1][2]

